1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,140
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,510
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,980
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:09,150
(Episode 15)

5
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:12,620
Oh, welcome.

6
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:14,820
Goodness.

7
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:18,290
But how did you two arrive together?

8
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,590
We met in front of the house.

9
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:22,860
Hello, Chairman Kim.

10
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:24,660
Hello to you too, Director Joo.

11
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,830
Thank you for coming,
especially with your sore leg.

12
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:29,370
Not at all.

13
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:30,570
You invited me
to such a special dinner.

14
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:31,640
Of course I had to come.

15
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,840
Seok Jin, it's been a while
since you've been here, hasn't it?

16
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:36,440
Oh, right.

17
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:38,340
I'm sorry I haven't been able
to visit more often.

18
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:40,850
Oh, please. We see each other
at the office every day.

19
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:43,520
Hi, Hae Ra.

20
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:47,320
Why act like it's been a while
when we talked on the phone earlier?

21
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,490
Why are you leaning on Seok Jin
instead of using crutches?

22
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:54,890
It's almost healed,
so I don't need them.

23
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:56,560
Is everyone here?

24
00:00:57,860 --> 00:00:58,900
Hello, sir.

25
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,500
I'm here as well, sir.

26
00:01:01,130 --> 00:01:02,730
Let's all go inside and have dinner.

27
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:05,040
Yes, let's head on in.

28
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:07,440
I'm all right, ma'am.

29
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:10,140
No, you must be careful
with your sore leg.

30
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:11,380
Go on in.

31
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:13,510
Careful.

32
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:16,950
Be rational.

33
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,660
How much do you think
Eun Seol will give me?

34
00:01:30,330 --> 00:01:32,900
Mom, don't get your hopes up.

35
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:35,900
You don't want
to be disappointed later on.

36
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:40,310
Won't she give me
at least 10,000 dollars?

37
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:42,870
You're hoping for that much?

38
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:46,740
Mom, you're something else.

39
00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:48,710
So you're saying
she won't even give me that?

40
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,750
When I didn't kick her to the curb?

41
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:54,050
Mom, let's be honest here.

42
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,350
You didn't really let her stay.

43
00:01:56,690 --> 00:01:59,020
She was the one who took you in.

44
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:01,130
What? Why you...

45
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:05,630
Hold on. Why have you been so quiet?

46
00:02:07,930 --> 00:02:09,230
- Grandma.
- Yes?

47
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:12,170
I'm sorry, but don't expect money
from Eun Seol.

48
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,210
Why not? Are you going
to bring up her hard work again?

49
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:17,340
It's not that.

50
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,980
She told me
to start my own business,

51
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:23,080
saying I can't keep working
part-time jobs forever.

52
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,280
Is Eun Seol putting up
the start-up money?

53
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,620
- Yes.
- How much?

54
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,990
Don't tell me...
The entire 50,000 dollars?

55
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,360
- Yes.
- So what did you say?

56
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:38,460
You said yes, right?

57
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,230
Of course I said no at first.

58
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:44,070
How could I possibly start
a business with her money?

59
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,500
But?

60
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,670
But in the end, she convinced me.

61
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:54,810
So I'm going to make
a lot of money...

62
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,280
and repay her several times over.

63
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,180
Good for you.

64
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:00,350
That's right.

65
00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:03,390
Of course a younger sister
should help her older brother.

66
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:06,020
She's finally pulling her weight.

67
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,630
I know she's my daughter,

68
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:11,330
but our Eun Seol is amazing.

69
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,870
You hurt your leg,
so please stay seated.

70
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:24,640
- But I can't just...
- It's fine,

71
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:25,740
so please sit.

72
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:27,750
Sure.

73
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:32,780
So...

74
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:35,450
Eun Seol, tell us about your family.

75
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,520
Who are you living with now?

76
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:42,530
My father, my older brother,
and my grandmother.

77
00:03:42,830 --> 00:03:45,330
What about your mom? You had one.

78
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,470
She passed away.

79
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:49,300
She passed away?

80
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:59,410
How dare you hit my daughter?
Do you have any idea who you are?

81
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,150
When?

82
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:05,250
Ten years ago.

83
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:07,490
Why? How did she die?

84
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,550
Hae Ra.

85
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:13,390
Why pry into someone's personal life
when it isn't your business?

86
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:14,790
It's rude.

87
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:18,930
Everyone, please have some tea.
You have some too, Eun Seol.

88
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,270
Yes, thank you.

89
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:25,000
So when does she start?

90
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:28,210
After next week's awards ceremony,

91
00:04:28,270 --> 00:04:30,410
I expect her to start
the following week.

92
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:32,140
An awards ceremony?

93
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:35,410
She was chosen
after such fierce competition.

94
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,150
Of course we should have one.

95
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:40,820
Please invite your family
to come as well.

96
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:43,320
Yes, thank you, ma'am.

97
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:47,230
Have you received her resume
and personal documents?

98
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:50,760
No. Not yet.

99
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:53,130
Just send them to me
before the ceremony.

100
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:56,030
Sure thing.

101
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:00,300
Well, we should be going now.

102
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,170
All right. Get home safely.

103
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:06,140
Seok Jin,
why don't you see Eun Seol home?

104
00:05:06,210 --> 00:05:07,450
Her leg must hurt.

105
00:05:07,650 --> 00:05:08,880
- Well...
- No, Mom.

106
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:09,980
I already called a taxi.

107
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:11,720
Let's go. It should be here by now.

108
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,550
But...

109
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:20,560
Thank you so much
for inviting me today.

110
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,030
Well then, good night.

111
00:05:22,930 --> 00:05:24,960
I'll see you at the office.

112
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,300
Sure.

113
00:05:33,770 --> 00:05:34,770
Come on.

114
00:05:42,450 --> 00:05:43,450
Attorney Seo.

115
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,380
Eun Seol.

116
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:52,360
Aren't you coming back
from the CEO's house?

117
00:05:56,430 --> 00:05:58,200
Did something bad happen there?

118
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:01,300
Well, it's nothing bad, but...

119
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:05,440
Here, sit with me for a moment.

120
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:21,290
What is it? You can tell me.

121
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:28,360
They asked me to submit my resume
and personal documents.

122
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:30,430
And?

123
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:34,500
If I do, won't that expose
my criminal record?

124
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,300
Then both my win and my job offer
might be revoked.

125
00:06:41,410 --> 00:06:44,910
Oh, is that all?
That's nothing to worry about.

126
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:47,010
None of the paperwork you submit...

127
00:06:47,010 --> 00:06:48,780
will show any kind
of criminal record.

128
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,820
- Really?
- Yes.

129
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:55,020
Besides, under current law,
it's strictly illegal...

130
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:58,090
for a company to check
an employee's criminal record.

131
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,960
Unless someone looks into it,
no one will ever know.

132
00:07:03,290 --> 00:07:08,130
I see. That's a huge relief.
I was really worried about that.

133
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:11,070
So, is everything okay now?

134
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,140
Yes, thank you, Attorney Seo.

135
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:18,040
From now on,
if you have any concerns,

136
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,310
you can always talk to me.

137
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:20,580
Okay?

138
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:22,950
Yes. I will.

139
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,740
You must be tired.
Head in and get some rest.

140
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,770
Okay. Good night.

141
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:49,510
Right.

142
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:11,260
You're home.

143
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:14,030
You've been getting in late lately.

144
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:18,900
I was just talking
with Eun Seol out front.

145
00:08:19,870 --> 00:08:20,870
Hyun Jae.

146
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:25,080
You're not a kid anymore.

147
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:28,550
It's fine to catch feelings and all,

148
00:08:29,810 --> 00:08:31,220
but you need to think this through.

149
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:34,120
What are you talking about?

150
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,850
If not, never mind.

151
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,740
(Resume)

152
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,570
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

153
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,040
What's this?

154
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:59,210
She didn't work at all
and just collected certificates...

155
00:08:59,210 --> 00:09:00,710
for ten years?

156
00:09:09,490 --> 00:09:10,490
It's me.

157
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:12,690
Stop by my office
before going to the awards ceremony.

158
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:14,430
Is something wrong?

159
00:09:14,490 --> 00:09:16,490
Just come when I tell you.
What's with all the questions?

160
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:18,460
All right.

161
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:26,300
Ko Eun Seol.

162
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,310
She's really something else.

163
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:31,110
She's no pushover.

164
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,450
So are you just going to let her be?

165
00:09:35,050 --> 00:09:37,920
If I don't,
do you have a better idea?

166
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,350
What if we expose
her criminal record?

167
00:09:41,350 --> 00:09:42,350
What?

168
00:09:43,190 --> 00:09:45,890
If we leak her criminal record,
her win will be canceled,

169
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:47,460
along with her job offer.

170
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:49,890
That's not an option.

171
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:51,660
Why not?

172
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:54,670
Burning the whole house down
just to catch a mouse?

173
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:58,600
Bringing up that incident
won't do us any good.

174
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,970
I suppose you're right.

175
00:10:04,310 --> 00:10:05,540
That ruthless girl.

176
00:10:10,310 --> 00:10:11,320
What's this?

177
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,720
What else could it be?
It's my resume.

178
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:17,090
Is there something wrong with it?

179
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:20,460
Something is very wrong with it.

180
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:22,260
It has no work history.

181
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,400
What have you been doing
for the past ten years?

182
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:27,970
My resume speaks for itself.

183
00:10:28,330 --> 00:10:29,770
I was getting
all sorts of certifications.

184
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,800
You spent ten years
getting certifications...

185
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:35,110
without holding a single job?

186
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,810
Why? Isn't that allowed?

187
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,550
It's not forbidden,
but it's certainly not normal.

188
00:10:43,610 --> 00:10:45,550
That's not how normal people live.

189
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:48,250
Just because it's unconventional
doesn't mean it's wrong.

190
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:50,860
Besides, I won the competition,

191
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:52,320
and I was hired
through special recruitment.

192
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:54,160
What does it matter
that I don't have work experience?

193
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:57,360
Are you hiding something?

194
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:00,100
What?

195
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,770
You really are hiding something.

196
00:11:03,530 --> 00:11:06,470
What is it?
Just be honest and tell me.

197
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:08,770
What are you hiding?

198
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:13,080
I said, tell me.

199
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:19,080
I think you're overstepping
your bounds, Ms. Kang.

200
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:21,650
I know you're my superior,

201
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:24,720
but do I really have to share details
of my private life with you?

202
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:26,620
What?

203
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,160
Are we done here?

204
00:11:28,830 --> 00:11:29,990
I'll be going now.

205
00:11:30,830 --> 00:11:32,900
Hey, Ko Eun Seol. Stop right there.

206
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,140
She's hiding something.

207
00:11:39,570 --> 00:11:42,470
She wouldn't have
run off like that otherwise.

208
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:02,260
Choi Soo Jung. It's been a while.

209
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:06,500
Listen, I'm calling
because I wanted to ask you something.

210
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:09,230
You and Ko Eun Seol were close,
weren't you?

211
00:12:10,270 --> 00:12:12,840
Do you know what happened to her
after she was expelled?

212
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,210
No.

213
00:12:14,570 --> 00:12:17,270
I lost touch with her after that,
so I have no idea.

214
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,480
Why?

215
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:20,140
No reason.

216
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:24,050
Is there anyone who might know
what she's been up to?

217
00:12:24,250 --> 00:12:27,790
Or could you look into it for me?
I'll make it worth your while.

218
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:30,820
Right. Thanks.

219
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:40,430
Did you have lunch, Ms. Kang?

220
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,300
Where's Ji Woo?

221
00:12:42,570 --> 00:12:44,640
She went out earlier
to attend some business.

222
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Did she?

223
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,770
She's never around when I need her.

224
00:12:55,310 --> 00:12:58,620
No way.
Is this where Eun Seol works?

225
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:00,750
It is. Mom, this is nice.

226
00:13:00,850 --> 00:13:03,220
Eun Guk, why can't you work
at a place like this?

227
00:13:03,290 --> 00:13:05,120
I'd love to, Grandma.

228
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,530
Mom, people come here to work,

229
00:13:07,590 --> 00:13:09,330
not to pay off a settlement.

230
00:13:09,490 --> 00:13:11,400
Was that really necessary?

231
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:13,930
Hey, I'm going to the restroom.

232
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Sure.

233
00:13:15,270 --> 00:13:17,070
- Over there. Do you see it?
- Right.

234
00:13:17,070 --> 00:13:18,570
- Yes, I've got it.
- Good.

235
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:36,950
Hello, ma'am.

236
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:39,690
You must be Eun Seol's grandmother.

237
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:42,490
I am. And who might you be?

238
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:46,100
I'm a friend of Eun Seol's
from high school.

239
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,460
Plus, I'm her supervisor here.

240
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:49,470
Oh, is that so?

241
00:13:50,170 --> 00:13:52,840
We lost touch
for the past ten years,

242
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,470
so you can't imagine
how happy I was to see her here.

243
00:13:55,470 --> 00:13:57,170
I bet you were.

244
00:13:57,580 --> 00:14:00,740
Eun Seol must've had
a very hard time.

245
00:14:01,050 --> 00:14:02,710
Tell me about it.

246
00:14:02,810 --> 00:14:05,320
It's a wonder she survived
in such a rough place.

247
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:06,750
I know.

248
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:09,020
I can't imagine
how hard it must've been for her.

249
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:12,290
Still, she earned certifications
in that rough place...

250
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:14,460
and even landed
a great job like this.

251
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:17,360
I know she's my granddaughter,
but she's really something else.

252
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:20,230
She got her certifications
in a "rough" place?

253
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:22,970
I know.

254
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:26,300
By the way, where exactly
is this "rough place" you mentioned?

255
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,410
Didn't you know when you asked?

256
00:14:29,810 --> 00:14:32,380
Me? What would I know?

257
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,880
My gosh. It's nothing.

258
00:14:35,350 --> 00:14:36,880
Just forget I said anything.

259
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:39,150
Ma'am. Wait!

260
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:43,090
A rough place?

261
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:45,720
Certifications. Ten years.

262
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:48,590
What could it be?

263
00:14:54,670 --> 00:14:56,430
Ms. Kang, aren't you going
to the awards ceremony?

264
00:14:58,370 --> 00:15:00,470
She got her certifications
in a rough place.

265
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,010
What kind of place would that be?

266
00:15:02,710 --> 00:15:04,070
What kind of certifications?

267
00:15:04,210 --> 00:15:05,680
All kinds.

268
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,950
Fashion, cooking,
computers, you name it.

269
00:15:08,050 --> 00:15:09,280
And she did it all
over the course of ten years.

270
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:11,520
Does that ring a bell at all?

271
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:14,350
There's only one place
that comes to mind.

272
00:15:14,790 --> 00:15:15,790
One place?

273
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:17,420
Where's that?

274
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:18,560
Prison.

275
00:15:19,090 --> 00:15:21,390
- What? Prison?
- Yes.

276
00:15:25,230 --> 00:15:27,060
Hey, Soo Jung. Did you look into it?

277
00:15:28,330 --> 00:15:29,330
Right.

278
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:31,440
Yes.

279
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:33,100
What?

280
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:35,310
Are you serious?

281
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:47,150
(Cheongma Emerging Designer
Awards Ceremony)

282
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:50,350
And now, we will present
the grand prize.

283
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:52,920
Grand prize winner, Ko Eun Seol,

284
00:15:52,990 --> 00:15:54,530
please come forward.

285
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:07,770
(Cheongma Emerging Designer
Awards Ceremony)

286
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:12,510
Next, we'll take
a commemorative photo.

287
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:20,680
- Eun Seol, you look amazing.
- Dad.

288
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:27,520
(Cheongma Emerging Designer
Awards Ceremony)

289
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,470
(Cheongma Emerging Designer
Awards Ceremony)

290
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:38,840
Just a moment.

291
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:46,110
What do you think you're doing?

292
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,550
I have something urgent to say
to the CEO.

293
00:16:48,610 --> 00:16:51,680
Team Leader Kang,
I don't know what this is about,

294
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:53,120
but let's talk after the ceremony.

295
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:55,350
No. It'll be too late then.

296
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:58,190
What will be too late, Ms. Kang?

297
00:17:02,990 --> 00:17:06,600
Go on.
What's all this commotion about?

298
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:08,630
Ko Eun Seol's grand prize award...

299
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:10,930
should be revoked, sir.

300
00:17:10,930 --> 00:17:14,200
Kang Hae Ra,
what are you talking about?

301
00:17:14,970 --> 00:17:15,970
Why?

302
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:20,110
If you're asking me to revoke it,
you must have a valid reason.

303
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,550
Of course I do.

304
00:17:21,610 --> 00:17:22,780
What's the reason?

305
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:27,680
On what grounds?

306
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,520
Ko Eun Seol has a criminal record.

307
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:35,060
What?

308
00:17:40,430 --> 00:17:42,600
Today's grand prize winner,
Ko Eun Seol,

309
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:44,740
is an ex-convict...

310
00:17:45,370 --> 00:17:48,270
who served ten whole years
in prison.

311
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:20,770
Team Leader Kang rocked the boat.
What do we do?

312
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:23,270
What can we do?

313
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,210
Now that it's happened,
she'll have to be let go.

314
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:32,280
(Cheongma Emerging Designer
Awards Ceremony)

315
00:18:32,350 --> 00:18:33,880
Eun Seol, please tell us.

316
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:37,590
What did Hae Ra mean?

317
00:18:38,190 --> 00:18:39,890
An ex-convict?

318
00:18:40,490 --> 00:18:41,530
Is it true?

319
00:18:41,530 --> 00:18:43,190
It's true, Mom.

320
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:46,130
You stay quiet.
Let's hear it from her.

321
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:48,230
Tell us, Ms. Ko.

322
00:18:49,270 --> 00:18:50,470
Are you an ex-convict?

323
00:18:56,270 --> 00:18:58,310
I asked if you had
a criminal record.

324
00:19:00,910 --> 00:19:01,910
Yes.

325
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,180
But I was framed.

326
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:10,190
You call that an excuse, Ms. Ko?

327
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:13,760
I'm not making excuses.
I really was framed.

328
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,460
It's not just any record.
You went in for murder.

329
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:17,590
What?

330
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:22,200
Is what Hae Ra said true?

331
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:24,170
Did you serve time for murder?

332
00:19:29,070 --> 00:19:30,970
I'm asking if it's true.

333
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:34,080
Yes.

334
00:19:39,550 --> 00:19:40,550
Then...

335
00:19:42,390 --> 00:19:43,950
Were you framed for murder?

336
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,160
Yes.

337
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:50,360
Seok Jin.

338
00:19:51,090 --> 00:19:52,100
Chief Cha,

339
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,500
what are you doing?

340
00:19:54,770 --> 00:19:58,100
Because a court's ruling
isn't always the truth.

341
00:20:02,710 --> 00:20:06,740
Like Ms. Ko says,
it's possible she was framed.

342
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:07,980
Enough.

343
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,650
Whose murder were you in for?

344
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:14,420
I didn't kill anyone, sir.

345
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:16,320
Ma'am.

346
00:20:16,990 --> 00:20:18,990
I'm really not that kind of person.

347
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:20,720
Kang Hae Ra.

348
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,590
You seem to know everything already,
so you tell me.

349
00:20:24,630 --> 00:20:25,960
Whose murder was she in for?

350
00:20:29,530 --> 00:20:32,040
It's too horrible for me to say.

351
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,900
What should I do, Dad?

352
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,270
Her own mom.

353
00:20:48,050 --> 00:20:49,150
What?

354
00:20:49,390 --> 00:20:51,960
Isn't there anything we can do?

355
00:20:53,590 --> 00:20:54,660
I'll go there.

356
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:02,970
Sir.

357
00:21:03,970 --> 00:21:06,340
It's time for you
to make a decision.

358
00:21:07,770 --> 00:21:09,040
You must cancel the award...

359
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:12,080
so this scandal doesn't tarnish
Cheongma's image.

360
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:15,010
Instead of rashly revoking
the award,

361
00:21:16,710 --> 00:21:19,150
I think it'd be better to call
the head of the Legal Team...

362
00:21:19,150 --> 00:21:20,620
and review the legal issues first.

363
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:24,920
I suppose so.

364
00:21:24,990 --> 00:21:28,660
Team Leader Seo and Ko Eun Seol
know each other personally, sir.

365
00:21:29,590 --> 00:21:31,230
How do you know that, Director Joo?

366
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:35,730
I saw the two of them
together myself.

367
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:42,570
Hello, Director Joo.

368
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:44,010
It's been a while, Team Leader Seo.

369
00:21:50,250 --> 00:21:53,480
Hold on. It must be true,
seeing as she went quiet.

370
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:56,720
Then it's obvious Mr. Seo
will take Ko Eun Seol's side.

371
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,420
There's no point in even asking.

372
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:06,100
Seo Hyun Jae, head of Legal,
is here to see you regarding Ms. Ko.

373
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:08,000
Tell him we don't need to see him.

374
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:09,330
Still...

375
00:22:10,470 --> 00:22:12,840
He came all this way.
Let's hear him out, honey.

376
00:22:15,170 --> 00:22:16,670
Tell him to come in.

377
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:18,180
Yes, sir.

378
00:22:30,190 --> 00:22:31,820
What is it that you want to say?

379
00:22:32,190 --> 00:22:33,420
(Cheongma Emerging Designer
Awards Ceremony)

380
00:22:33,490 --> 00:22:35,190
I'd like a private word
with you, sir.

381
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:36,590
Why?

382
00:22:36,890 --> 00:22:38,930
Are you going to take her side
because you know her?

383
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:42,370
Would the outcome change
if I took her side?

384
00:22:42,630 --> 00:22:45,800
Is there a special reason
you must speak to the CEO alone?

385
00:22:46,840 --> 00:22:49,910
That is also something
I'd like to tell only the CEO.

386
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:51,340
Team Leader Seo.

387
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,440
All right. Come to my office.

388
00:22:55,150 --> 00:22:56,210
Dad!

389
00:22:57,850 --> 00:22:58,850
Attorney Seo...

390
00:23:01,620 --> 00:23:04,450
Eun Seol, I'll speak to the CEO.

391
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,120
But...

392
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:26,380
Goodness.

393
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:27,940
Ma'am.

394
00:23:38,090 --> 00:23:41,020
Don't even dream
of joining our company.

395
00:23:41,190 --> 00:23:42,190
No.

396
00:23:42,830 --> 00:23:44,830
I'm going to join this company
no matter what.

397
00:23:45,930 --> 00:23:47,060
So don't you try to stop me.

398
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:55,110
(Cheongma Emerging Designer
Awards Ceremony)

399
00:23:55,210 --> 00:23:56,970
Why the heck
are you taking her side?

400
00:23:58,310 --> 00:23:59,510
When did I take her side?

401
00:24:00,210 --> 00:24:02,980
You sounded like you believed
everything she said. Am I wrong?

402
00:24:03,380 --> 00:24:05,320
So should I just blindly suspect her
like you do?

403
00:24:06,450 --> 00:24:08,120
We need to figure out
the situation first.

404
00:24:11,690 --> 00:24:13,690
What's there to figure out?

405
00:24:13,690 --> 00:24:15,760
She rotted in prison for ten years!

406
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,330
All right. Out with it.

407
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:22,200
What about Ko Eun Seol
did you want to tell me?

408
00:24:23,970 --> 00:24:26,640
Sir, Ms. Ko was framed.

409
00:24:27,740 --> 00:24:29,440
She already told me that,

410
00:24:29,970 --> 00:24:31,140
but I don't believe her.

411
00:24:32,140 --> 00:24:35,910
I can bet not just my legal career,
but everything I have on it.

412
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:39,480
She was definitely framed, sir.

413
00:24:40,250 --> 00:24:41,820
Even if that were true,

414
00:24:41,890 --> 00:24:43,750
that's not
what's important right now.

415
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:45,720
The problem is that
she's a convicted felon.

416
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:48,190
One who killed her own mother.

417
00:24:50,830 --> 00:24:53,260
I have no intention
of stirring up trouble.

418
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:55,070
I'll let her keep the grand prize...

419
00:24:55,470 --> 00:24:57,170
and also give her the prize money.

420
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,870
What about hiring her?

421
00:25:00,670 --> 00:25:01,710
Are you telling me...

422
00:25:02,270 --> 00:25:05,240
to hire someone
convicted of matricide?

423
00:25:05,710 --> 00:25:07,240
There were no restrictions
on eligibility,

424
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:09,650
and we heavily promoted
the blind screening process.

425
00:25:10,050 --> 00:25:12,050
This could lead to a pointless
discrimination controversy.

426
00:25:12,820 --> 00:25:16,250
Cheongma regulations state that
anyone who served prison time...

427
00:25:16,490 --> 00:25:17,790
is ineligible to apply.

428
00:25:17,820 --> 00:25:19,320
Aren't you familiar
with that policy?

429
00:25:20,660 --> 00:25:22,360
That applies to standard hiring.

430
00:25:22,930 --> 00:25:24,190
There were no such
restrictive clauses...

431
00:25:24,190 --> 00:25:25,760
in this competition's guidelines.

432
00:25:27,530 --> 00:25:31,070
Are you telling me
we should just hire Ko Eun Seol?

433
00:25:33,100 --> 00:25:34,100
Yes.

434
00:25:34,570 --> 00:25:35,840
That's ridiculous.

435
00:25:36,340 --> 00:25:38,940
I can't have a murderer
as a Cheongma employee.

436
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:41,210
So go and make this clear
to Ko Eun Seol.

437
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,780
Tell her to be satisfied
with her prize money...

438
00:25:43,850 --> 00:25:44,850
and back off quietly.

439
00:25:45,780 --> 00:25:49,490
Sir, if we do that,
she may take legal action.

440
00:25:50,850 --> 00:25:52,690
What? Legal action?

441
00:25:53,660 --> 00:25:56,560
Then isn't it your job
to defend us against it, Mr. Seo?

442
00:25:57,930 --> 00:25:58,930
Why?

443
00:25:59,260 --> 00:26:01,530
Are you going to defend her
instead of the company?

444
00:26:02,730 --> 00:26:04,900
If so, you should resign first.

445
00:26:05,740 --> 00:26:06,740
Sir.

446
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:09,940
Tell her to take legal action
or do whatever she wants.

447
00:26:11,910 --> 00:26:12,910
Is there anything else?

448
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:15,310
If not, you can leave.

449
00:26:19,980 --> 00:26:21,250
I said you were dismissed.

450
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:24,320
Right, sir.

451
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:35,530
Legal action?

452
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:41,100
Thankfully, we got to know
the real Ko Eun Seol...

453
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:42,510
before it was too late.

454
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:46,480
I know.

455
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:50,380
How could she do that
to her own mother of all people?

456
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:52,020
It's horrible.

457
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:57,690
Do you really think she did it?

458
00:26:58,520 --> 00:27:00,260
She says she was framed.

459
00:27:01,990 --> 00:27:03,360
And you believe her?

460
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:05,260
You don't, Director Joo?

461
00:27:05,660 --> 00:27:08,300
The look in her eyes
didn't suggest she was lying.

462
00:27:09,570 --> 00:27:12,300
That's because you see her
in a positive light, ma'am.

463
00:27:12,940 --> 00:27:13,940
According to Hae Ra,

464
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:16,540
Ko Eun Seol was
a big troublemaker in school.

465
00:27:16,710 --> 00:27:19,180
She was even expelled
for setting fire to the Art Room.

466
00:27:21,080 --> 00:27:22,080
Really?

467
00:27:22,780 --> 00:27:23,780
Yes.

468
00:27:24,380 --> 00:27:25,580
And think about it.

469
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:28,420
Not just anyone can take on someone
with a knife.

470
00:27:31,190 --> 00:27:32,190
That's true.

471
00:27:33,490 --> 00:27:36,160
She's much more fearsome and vicious
than she looks.

472
00:27:37,260 --> 00:27:38,930
Nothing good will come
from associating with her,

473
00:27:39,100 --> 00:27:41,600
so stop paying her any mind, okay?

474
00:27:44,930 --> 00:27:45,970
All right.

475
00:27:46,940 --> 00:27:49,210
And you must not let her
join the company.

476
00:27:51,310 --> 00:27:52,410
I said I get it.

477
00:27:57,780 --> 00:27:59,680
Oh, my goodness.

478
00:28:01,120 --> 00:28:02,720
I knew this would happen.

479
00:28:03,220 --> 00:28:06,660
I knew from the start
something like this would happen.

480
00:28:06,820 --> 00:28:09,130
So what happens now?

481
00:28:09,490 --> 00:28:11,060
Does this mean
Eun Seol can't get the job?

482
00:28:11,930 --> 00:28:13,160
I don't know.

483
00:28:13,830 --> 00:28:15,670
Attorney Seo said he'd talk to them.

484
00:28:16,030 --> 00:28:17,030
We'll have to wait and see.

485
00:28:17,900 --> 00:28:19,440
Wait for what?

486
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:24,610
Even the attorney's grandfather
couldn't bail her out of this mess.

487
00:28:24,910 --> 00:28:26,280
Mom, why have you been
acting like this?

488
00:28:26,340 --> 00:28:28,080
It's like you're hoping
for the worst.

489
00:28:28,140 --> 00:28:29,950
I'm just upset, that's all.

490
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:33,450
We were all humiliated
in front of everyone.

491
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:38,320
But who the heck
was that girl from before?

492
00:28:39,590 --> 00:28:40,590
Who?

493
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:43,460
The brat who exposed
Eun Seol's criminal record.

494
00:28:44,190 --> 00:28:47,160
She's Eun Seol's supervisor,
and they went to high school together.

495
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,870
How do you know that, Mom?

496
00:28:50,530 --> 00:28:53,640
How else?
I ran into her in the restroom.

497
00:28:54,600 --> 00:28:57,010
She's a real fox, that one.

498
00:28:57,370 --> 00:28:59,240
The way she was trying
to sound me out...

499
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:02,410
What do you mean by that, Grandma?
Sound you out about what?

500
00:29:03,150 --> 00:29:05,750
What? It's nothing.

501
00:29:06,380 --> 00:29:08,520
Mom, did you say something?

502
00:29:09,850 --> 00:29:12,290
What? What would I say?

503
00:29:12,720 --> 00:29:15,020
Did you tell her
about Eun Seol's criminal record?

504
00:29:15,390 --> 00:29:18,130
What? Are you crazy?
As if I would say that.

505
00:29:18,260 --> 00:29:19,360
Then why are you stuttering?

506
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:22,530
Be honest, Mom.
You messed up, didn't you?

507
00:29:22,670 --> 00:29:24,030
I told you I didn't.

508
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:26,800
She seemed like
she was feeling me out,

509
00:29:26,870 --> 00:29:29,770
so I kept my mouth zipped shut.

510
00:29:29,970 --> 00:29:32,510
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

511
00:29:35,510 --> 00:29:37,480
I figured I should hear
the full story from you directly.

512
00:29:39,550 --> 00:29:42,050
Your mother was murdered by someone,

513
00:29:43,220 --> 00:29:44,690
and you got framed for it?

514
00:29:47,090 --> 00:29:48,090
Yes.

515
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:51,590
And you were imprisoned
for ten years?

516
00:29:54,900 --> 00:29:55,900
Yes.

517
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:02,540
Did you ever think
to reach out to me,

518
00:30:02,540 --> 00:30:03,540
even after you got out?

519
00:30:10,850 --> 00:30:13,980
You were the one person
I couldn't bring myself to contact.

520
00:30:16,520 --> 00:30:17,650
I was too scared.

521
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,320
You should've just told me.

522
00:30:20,390 --> 00:30:22,660
You can't just
cut someone off like that.

523
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:27,330
I waited.

524
00:30:33,870 --> 00:30:35,040
I'm so sorry.

525
00:30:43,750 --> 00:30:44,980
It must've been
so hard for you, Eun Seol.

526
00:30:47,320 --> 00:30:48,320
Seok Jin...

527
00:30:52,520 --> 00:30:54,620
- Chief Cha.
- Ms. Joo.

528
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:01,730
What is Ko Eun Seol doing here?

529
00:31:36,600 --> 00:31:40,400
(A Trap Called Desire)

530
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:43,040
From now on,
discuss things like that with me first.

531
00:31:43,470 --> 00:31:45,410
This is Ko Eun Seol.
Do you remember me?

532
00:31:45,710 --> 00:31:47,340
There's a favor I need to ask you.

533
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:49,250
Were you the one behind this?

534
00:31:49,510 --> 00:31:50,680
There's nothing to worry about.

535
00:31:50,980 --> 00:31:52,620
What can some
low-level designer accomplish...

536
00:31:52,620 --> 00:31:54,120
just by getting into Cheongma?

537
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:56,750
Why aren't you answering?
Don't tell me you did it.

538
00:31:57,490 --> 00:31:59,820
What are your plans with my Hae Ra?

539
00:32:00,090 --> 00:32:02,030
You're not actually thinking
of marrying her, are you?

540
00:32:02,430 --> 00:32:04,060
You think I'm going
to let this slide?

541
00:32:04,660 --> 00:32:06,360
Officially, it was a mistake.

542
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:08,700
Unofficially, it's payback
for what you did.

543
00:32:09,130 --> 00:32:10,770
Are you saying that
one of the people here...

544
00:32:10,770 --> 00:32:12,370
is the culprit we're looking for?

545
00:32:13,070 --> 00:32:15,070
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
